      id: 'tqlFullUWGuidelines-181',
      section: 'NOTES RECEIVABLE INCOME',
      headingLevel: 4,
      content: `**§ 1.8.4.12**

Note receivable income may be used for qualifying income subject to the following:
- Verify that the income can be expected to continue for a minimum of three (3) years from the date of the
mortgage application.
- Obtain a copy of the Note to establish the amount and length of payment.
- Document regular receipt of income for the most recent 12-months using either cancelled checks, bank
statements, or federal tax returns.
- Payments on a Note executed within the past 12-months, regardless of the duration, may not be used as
stable income.`,
      sourceDocId: 'tqlFullUWGuidelines',
      chunkIndex: 181,
