      section: 'TIP INCOME',
      headingLevel: 4,
      content: `**§ 1.8.4.22**

Tips and gratuity income may be considered if the receipt of such income is typical for the borrower's occupation
(i.e., waitperson, taxi driver, etc.). Tip income should be received for at least two (2) years.
Documentation will be based upon the documentation type selected (12- or 24- months). Obtain one (1) or two
years of federal income tax returns along with a year-to-date paystub. Income should be averaged over the
time-period verified. If the tip income is not reported on the paystubs or tax returns, then it may not be included in
qualifying income.`,
